WEBVTT

00:00:01.290 --> 00:00:02.671
Hi, I'm Gardenia!

00:00:02.671 --> 00:00:07.736
Liquid time-constant networks came from neuroscience, Gated DeltaNet from efficient Transformers.

00:00:07.736 --> 00:00:09.578
They're the same recurrence.

00:00:09.578 --> 00:00:10.959
Let's derive it.

00:00:12.308 --> 00:00:16.627
Step the liquid network's equation with its own fused solver, and out

00:00:16.627 --> 00:00:21.306
comes a state that decays by an input-dependent factor: a gated linear recurrence.

00:00:22.817 --> 00:00:26.619
Rearrange one step of the solver, and the whole update reads like this.

00:00:27.038 --> 00:00:30.878
The old state is scaled by alpha bar, a number between zero and one.

00:00:31.298 --> 00:00:34.506
Then a write: the gate's output, pulling the state toward a target.

00:00:34.926 --> 00:00:39.361
And alpha bar depends on the input, through the gate: the same

00:00:39.361 --> 00:00:42.318
data-dependent alpha as Mamba2, Gated DeltaNet and KDA.

00:00:43.733 --> 00:00:46.623
But gating alone multiplies the whole state by one number.

00:00:46.623 --> 00:00:50.090
It can clear the table, but not pick up a single plate.

00:00:50.510 --> 00:00:55.223
The gated delta rule adds targeted erasure: alpha decays everything, beta wipes

00:00:55.223 --> 00:00:57.187
the current key before writing.

00:00:59.217 --> 00:01:04.031
A new implementation, LTCAttention, puts the time constant on the attention score.

00:01:04.031 --> 00:01:08.844
The block's first token sets a bounded time constant per learned direction.

00:01:09.264 --> 00:01:12.966
Along each direction, a key's weight decays with its age.

00:01:12.966 --> 00:01:17.408
Folded into queries and keys, standard attention stays the only quadratic step.

00:01:19.217 --> 00:01:23.955
It wins per token, across three seeds, but runs twelve point four percent slower.

00:01:23.955 --> 00:01:27.001
Spent on baseline training, that could match the gain.

00:01:28.350 --> 00:01:32.483
Tau, alpha and a half-life are one number in three coordinate systems.

00:01:32.483 --> 00:01:34.894
The delta rule is what gating adds.

00:01:36.775 --> 00:01:41.060
To recap: one recurrence in two notations, a delta rule that erases

00:01:41.060 --> 00:01:44.274
one fact, and a hybrid awaiting a wall-clock test.

00:01:44.694 --> 00:01:46.917
Every source is in the full article.

00:01:46.917 --> 00:01:47.552
I'm Gardenia.

00:01:47.552 --> 00:01:47.869
Bye!
